I should have know before I started that this year would not yield me
more than a runner up score, like the 4 times before. It doesn't seem
to matter if I go for highest class score or lowest ascended score.
There should be a trophy for becoming second. Any idea how hard that
would be? :-)

Even though I do not play any Nethack during the year, it does start to
itch when november is coming. Lately I have been spending most of my
free time playing WoW. Therefor I decided to start another pacifist and
improve my 2003 pacifist score (I lost with just a few 100 score).

This time I would not use the oracle to get to lvl 3 and would not
identify anything by using it other than a scroll of identify. And I
would take special care not to oil any squeeky boards :-)

Yeti-Hea-Gno-Fem-Neu's tale:

I found 9 lamps in mine town (2 of them magic). Even though I prefer
silver scale + magic cloak, I feel really uncomfortable without magic
protect so I got archon + gray dragon scale mail.
In one of the general stores I also got a leash.

My pet archon Desiderata didn't like the shopkeepers very much so I had
soon maxed out my divine ac.

In the mines I had my first level teleport trap accident. There are no
words I fear more than "Desiderata suddenly disappears from sight. Your
leash goes slack". Fortunately the mines are a short branch so I found
her in time.

But fear had crept into me so I decided to skip the mines (guaranteed
polymorph trap) and head for Sokoban.

In Sokoban I did everything wrong that could go wrong. Used pick-axe
and scroll of earth several times. But I never can point out what luck
exactly does so I decided to ignore this factor.

Sokoban gave me a bag of holding. Nice!

I went down fast. Dug down on Medusa's level. Went up and let
Desiderata deal with her and so I got a shield of reflection. Went down
again and (using conflict even though not really necessary) got to the
wand of wishing.

By then I had only genocided 'c' as my pet doesn't attack them and they
can become really annoying standing in the way.

I spent most of the wishing charges on Orb of Fate (half damage,
warning, luckstone, level teleport). I knew of 2 artifacts in the game
already (Sunsword on archon and Frost brand on dlvl 1) but there might
have been more. After recharge I finally got it. This item makes the
life of a pacifist so much easier!

Because of all the wishes I spent on the Orb I had but 1 left for the
rest of my ascencion kit. I decided to wait a bit until I got more
items.

Going back up I had my second level teleport incident. It was next to a
stairs up (hadn't discovered it on my way down). I used my last wish on
a ring of teleport control. Went to lvl 1 and dug my way down while
being blindfolded. Finally finding her on the level right above from
where I lost her :-(

Still being lvl 1 I did some alchemy to boost my hitpoints to 70 or so.

Back in the castle (where I usually keep my stash) I polypiled all the
armor to get T-shirt, gauntlets of dex, boots of water walking (my
favourite because accidents do happen), cloak of displacement and
jumping boots.

That is when I decided to let this character rest a bit (was busy
organizing raid party to kill Majordomo in WoW).

I almost forgot about nethack when on 30th of november I decided to
give it a shot even though I was still lvl 1. I decided to take it 1
goal at a time and see where I would end up.

I became lvl 14 quickly by foocubus dancing and reverse genociding
wraiths. The Cyclops was easy. (The poor man forgot to pick up the
staff of Aesculapius, so I did it for him).

I genocided t and w (I really fear them).

Then I went down fast. Vlad was easy as always. Amulet of life saving.

Asmodeus was more of a problem. I think because I was using conflict
that he became angry and didn't let me bribe him. With him being lvl 49
there was no way my lvl 31 archon would attack him. Believe me I have
had more patience than a Chinese grinder but no matter how often I
would hit him down to like 5 hps with the staff my archon would not
attack. Also the staff doesn't drain levels from Asmodeus. He stayed on
lvl 49. After a lot of time trying I decided to leave him be and
continue.

Juiblex was easy (he didn't even swallow me).

I removed conflict and bribed Baalzebub.

I teleported down to VS (lvl 47) and on that level I had my third level
teleport trap accident. Fortunately when I finally found her she was
still my pet.

Going back up I found Orcus. Desiderata knew how to handle him. Mapping
all the levels was tedious as I couldn't get my "magic mapping" fail
chance lower than 93%. So I only mapped it the hard way or the
occasional blessed scroll of magic mapping.

I had been playing from 17:00 straight. It was 03:00 at this point.
Fortunately I was playing on the German server so I had until 09:00 in
the morning but I was getting kinda sleepy.

When I am sleepy I make mistakes. So i lost my only cream pie in a
stupid move. I went back to get more in mine town (only living
shopkeeper to steal from). But when I got there I totally forgot what I
was going to do there and assumed it was to see if there was anything
worthwhile in my first stash to take with me before attacking Wizard of
Yendor. So after I had taken all I thought useful I went back up the
mines and ran into a kobold zombie. Having 18/20 Str means bye bye
pacifist conduct. I wasn't totally devastated because I already
ascended a pacifist 2 years ago and I was just competing for lowest
score.

I went back down and got the Book of the Dead from the wizard and did
the invocation. When I finally had the amulet it was 4 am. Normally the
wizard pops up during the fight with the high priest bit not this time.
Geryon appeared out of nowhere but he could be bribed.

Going up went very smooth. I got teleported down only 1 time. I had no
problem bypassing Asmodeus. But I had another big problem because of
the time pressure. Normally I collect/polypile potions just to make
sure I have plenty for my pet. Not this time, so very soon my archon
refused to attack the wizard. As it was already nearing 5 am my bed was
getting more important than the score I would get. So I decided to use
a wand of death on him.

The planes were easier than ever (portal on earth and fire was
extremely close and air and water went very fast).

In the end I ended up killing the wizard 3 times (bad, bad). I
inspected the middle altar first (Death) but I didn't go near it. When
I could see it I inspected it and it said "aligned". I was so tired
that I confused this with "lawful". When I got to the left altar I
noticed this mistake when that one also turned out to be "aligned".
doh. When I stood on it I found out that it was chaotic. I did have a
helmet of opposite alignment with me but I am unsure what happens for
neutral chars. I assume I will still lose my divine ac. Not very funny
when you have to go throughs hordes of angry priests to another altar.
So I decided to go back to my first altar and that turned out to be the
correct one.

I finished my game at 6 am and I am pretty sure I will not get the
Nethack itch any time soon!

I never found a magic whistle, speed boots or helm of brilliance.
I didn't genocide R, h, ;, L (which I normally do, but I didn't have
markers left)

I ended up with 66456 points and of course as runner up. This time I do
not feel as bad as I had the excuse of time pressure. The only reason I
can think of why living legend Marvin decided to go for "Lowest Scored
Ascencion" is that otherwise I would have been no1 and the RNG doesn't
seem to permit that :-)

